    style(lint): reformat the two tracked files the tree-wide ruff-format arm reds on
    
    `ruff format --check .` at f43a602 printed "Would reformat: scripts/master_doc_panel.py,
    scripts/node-bus-worker.py" (2 files would be reformatted, 39 already formatted), so
    `gitreins guard --full` at that tip answered Tier 1 Guards: FAIL on the lint arm. Because
    this repo's lint lane grades the whole tree rather than the diff, that red refused the
    Tier-1 lane of every closure regardless of which file was staged, and it is what blocked
    closing CF-374 on a green gate.
    
    The two offenders are formatting-only: `ruff format` rewrote argument lists, call
    signatures and string concatenation; `ruff check .` was "All checks passed!" before and
    after, and `git diff --ignore-all-space` is empty against the pre-fix blobs in the sense
    that no token changed (reviewed hunk by hunk: line wrapping and one blank line after the
    module docstring in each file). No executable statement was altered.
    
    CF-258 is the live row for this class and names scripts/node_seed.py; that file is already
    ruff-format clean at f43a602 (`ruff format --check scripts/node_seed.py` -> 1 file already
    formatted), so its named member had been fixed while the class stayed live through these
    two other files. This commit clears the class: `ruff format --check .` now reads
    "41 files already formatted" with no Would reformat line, `ruff check .` is clean, and
    `gitreins guard --full` answers Tier 1 Guards: PASS (secrets clean, lint ok, tests full).
    
    Gates: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (rc=0) at this tree.
    CI: none configured for coding-hermes/code-factory (gh run list -> []).
    
    ch:trace: row=CF-258 evidence=.gitreins/logs/guard-20261106T093037.082550Z.log test=tests/selftest.sh
